<Stub
  title="AI and authorship — Evan DeLord"
  description="How AI is used on this website and how articles written by Evan are identified."
  label="Authorship"
  heading="AI and authorship"
>
  <AuthorNote>
  <p>The website is built by Claude Code or Codex models according to my tastes. I aim to put the substantive content in my own human words with only minor spelling, grammar, and clarity feedback from AI models. However, this is an AI-generated site, so <strong>by default, assume the words have come from AI models</strong>, and I'll indicate which articles are written by me with an “-Evan” signoff and I'll use a dark green left border for individual passages written by me.</p>
  <p>As much as I'd like to write all the words by hand, good writing takes time. I'll focus on hand-writing (or typing) the content where the writing process would help me think through the subject matter or when AI text would just seem inappropriate (like this statement).</p>
  <p>I encourage anyone to check my work or any other work with a reliable tool like <a href="https://www.pangram.com/">https://www.pangram.com/</a> for assessing whether content was generated by a human or AI.</p>
  </AuthorNote>
</Stub>
